I find it's "n/a" in \pump\omnipod-dash\src\main\java\info\nightscout\androidaps\plugins\pump\omnipod\dash\OmnipodDashPumpPlugin.kt (1041-1044)
`    override fun serialNumber(): String {
        return podStateManager.uniqueId?.toString()
            ?: "n/a" // TODO i18n
    }
`
I tried "n/a" and it worked 😄 😄 
If the result of podStateManager.uniqueId?.toString() is null, it returns the string "n/a" as a default value. Can this be added to the documentation? When there is no active pump connection(e.g. after the previous pump has expired but no new pump has been connected yet). the password will be reset to "n/a".
